                <pb facs="0141" n="131" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg131"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710 Consultation 3/65: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Braden</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-19T22:00:00-05:00">December 19, 1941—10
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>518. Please express to the Foreign Minister the Department’s sincere appreciation
                    for the information he has furnished you regarding the attitude of the Peruvian
                    and Ecuadoran representatives in Bogotá with regard to the boundary dispute and
                    the forthcoming consultative meeting. Recent developments make it possible that
                    some agreement at least in principle between the two countries may solve this
                    problem prior to January 15, the date of the Rio meeting. If, however, no
                    agreement is reached, the Department will bear very much in mind the helpful
                    suggestions of Dr. López de Mesa.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
